    "description": "STG, Inc. is a federal government contractor headquartered in Reston, VA and is SEI CMMI Maturity Level 3 Rated, ISO 9001:2008 Certified and ISO/IEC 20000-1:2011 Certified.  \n \nWorking as the main web developer responsible for the corporate website, Intranet and 7 other websites. \n \nDeveloped the corporate websites for STG, Inc using Ruby 1.9.2 - 2.0 and Rails 3.2 – 4.0. \n \nDeveloped an enterprise Lead Tracking System that was designed for the company top executives and the sales team to keep track of all customers, opportunities, and bid status through the entire federal bid lifecycle. It contained a dashboard and reports reviewed by the executives to make critical business decisions. \n \nDevelopment of responsive websites using Ruby on Rails, Bootstrap, Foundation, jQuery, JavaScript, HTML5, CSS3, ColdFusion, PHP,MySQL, MS SQL, MS SQL Server.  \n \nAdministration of Apache web servers running on Enterprise Linux with 10 deployed websites. Responsible of Linux security updates and hack prevention on the in-house web servers. Administration of Windows IIS servers.  \n \nOptimize websites using tools like PageSpeed to analyze possible bottlenecks and decrease website load times. Converted our corporate website into the fastest loading website compared to our competition.  \n \nCertified as internal ISO and CMMI auditor.  \n \nResearch, test, evaluate, and deploy commercial applications as well as in-house developed applications programs.  \n \nDevelop and maintain the Software Development Plan. Plan, assign, and direct the activities of designers, developers, and systems analysts.  \n \nE-commerce website development with smart shopping cart and client login using ColdFusion and MS SQL backend (ECSIII).  \n \nConverted EPA National Directory software to a web based interactive application with ColdFusion frontend and Oracle 8i backend. Still in use today by the EPA.",
